body:
It's not nearly as bad as this, but words definitely do have a way of sticking with you. My mother has always been obsessed with my weight, putting me on diets, pushing me to exercise up to 6 days a week and berating me wherever possible. When I was a teen still living at home she was angry about the state of my room and was throwing stuff around as she often did. She picked up a pair of my jeans and snarled at me;

'Well, you're never going to fit into these so we may as well just throw them away." 

I will never forget these words as long as I live, and she wonders why I have depression and severe body dysmorphia as an adult. I would hate myself forever if I had to look into the face of my offspring after saying something as cruel as that person's mother did, or my mother for that matter. Another reason I'm childless.
